// Ch5 B05 "Lanternfall, part 2: the weir" (act1_ch05.md; the Kerrid beat). Letterboxed. The sea-cut
// weir: the boats tip over the last stone lip one after another and the sea-glow takes them.
// P11 (from the sea side, low): a child leans out after her snagged boat and slips; a big hand in a
// wrapped sleeve takes her by the collar and sets her back on the step. No line. He is already
// looking out to sea. P12 (the two-shot on the weir step): he sees Asha's face in the lamplight and
// goes still (gesture slot). Toma's line to Rhen; Kerrid's head turns at "Sallow" (one look, 1.0 s).
// The one line to Asha; her patience. Toma, courteous and wary. Kerrid falls in last (P11 again);
// kerrid_stair enters. Sets ch05_met_kerrid; the chapter flow joins him to the roster.
// Watches, every one (ADR 0017, ADR 0020 (b) and (d), ADR 0022 (g)):
//   - Kerrid has exactly three lines in Ch5, all here: the one to Asha, his name, and Corrow.
//     He says nothing to Rhen anywhere in the chapter; every Kerrid beat with Rhen is a gesture.
//   - No glow on his hands at all, in any shot, and no close-up on his hands (no @vfx at kerrid).
//   - Toma does not know the face: a guardian sizing up a big armed man, no recognition.
//   - Nobody names Corrow's dead captain; nobody hails him or calls him a legend.
//   - He asks nothing and is invited to nothing; he simply falls in at the back of the line.
title: ch05_lanternfall_weir
location: ch05/pemakar
---
@camera P11
@sfx weir_spill
@anim weir_child lean_out
@wait 0.8
@anim weir_child slip
@anim kerrid catch_collar weir_child
@wait 1.0
@anim kerrid look_at sea
@wait 1.0
@camera P12
@mark asha weir_step walk
@wait 0.6
@anim kerrid look_at asha
@wait 1.2
@anim rhen slip
Toma [worried]: Rhen Sallow, if you fall in that channel I am not coming in after you. #line:ch05_weir_001
@anim kerrid look_at rhen
@wait 1.0
@anim kerrid look_at asha
@wait 0.6
Kerrid as "???" [neutral]: I held a stair for your mother once. #line:ch05_weir_002
@face asha neutral 0.2
@wait 0.8
Asha [tender]: Where? #line:ch05_weir_003
@anim kerrid look_at sea
@wait 1.5
Asha [soft_smile]: ...Then another time. #line:ch05_weir_004
@mark toma weir_guard walk
Toma [neutral]: Your name, sir? #line:ch05_weir_005
Kerrid [neutral]: Kerrid. #line:ch05_weir_006
Toma [neutral]: And where are you bound? #line:ch05_weir_007
Kerrid [neutral]: Corrow. #line:ch05_weir_008
Toma [neutral]: The Lady Cantor's road goes by Corrow. #line:ch05_weir_009
@wait 1.5
Ysolde [neutral]: Then he will be walking our way whether we like it or not. #line:ch05_weir_010
Asha [soft_smile]: He's going where we're going, Toma. #line:ch05_weir_011
@camera P11
@music kerrid_stair fade=2.0
@mark asha line_head walk
@mark kerrid line_tail walk
@wait 1.5
@anim rhen walk_backwards
Rhen [smile]: Does the old man come with the town, or did we just collect him? #line:ch05_weir_012
Asha [neutral]: Rhen. #line:ch05_weir_013
<<set $ch05_met_kerrid = true>>
@letterbox off
===
